{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38149-is-professional-training-a-demon-merit-or-a-cover-merit","id":38149,"title":"Is Professional Training a Demon Merit, or a Cover Merit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-27T20:22:42-08:00","id":38149,"title":"Is Professional Training a Demon Merit, or a Cover Merit?","content":"I'm undecided.<br /> Here are the factors I've considered.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b>:<br /> - It gives you Skill Specialities<br /> - It gives you a free skill dot<br /> - It gives you a beat for spending XP. (and when you spend XP you are not really in character at all.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cover:</b><br /> - Demon's don't thematically have Jobs, or Professions, covers do.<br /> - It gives you contacts, and not generally the sort of contact you would want knowing you are a Demon<br /> - It feels very appropriate to gain it using the Legend ability of Cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Not Both:</b><br /> - You can only take profession once, so if you have it on the same Demon as a Demon Merit, and on his Cover, you might end up with 2 different Professions<br /> (I'm not sure that you can't take profession twice, actually)<br /> <br /> <br /> Right now I am leaning towards Demon,<br /> and on Cover it just doesn't mechanically make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T22:55:06-08:00","id":38171,"title":"","content":"It could be either, it really depends on the context. In most cases I would go with Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T23:22:58-08:00","id":38175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38149-is-professional-training-a-demon-merit-or-a-cover-merit?p=38171#post38171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be either, it really depends on the context. In most cases I would go with Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate why?<br /> <br /> Also how you overcome the various issues I mentioned?<br /> (Like where the free skill dot goes, when do you get the bonus beat for upping a skill?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T06:19:29-08:00","id":38265,"title":"","content":"Social merits tend to be cover-related. I'd make the Contacts Cover related, but I would make the actual Professional Training something the Demon has, to protect it from going poof and leaving you with an inexplicable extra skill point. Demons don't tend to forget things, and it's a merit tied up in being trained to do a task, so it'd make a lot of sense if they /don't/ magically forget how to do a job between Covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T06:42:05-08:00","id":38269,"title":"","content":"you got a good point there as the profiessional training is mental / physical training and the demons have a perfect memory anyway there !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T23:31:26-08:00","id":38620,"title":"","content":"It also depends on if you're doing complex or simplified covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T03:40:33-08:00","id":38666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38149-is-professional-training-a-demon-merit-or-a-cover-merit?p=38620#post38620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also depends on if you're doing complex or simplified covers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously full cover rules.<br /> Simplified covers are a side bar option rule. (One that I really find misguided)<br /> With similified covers you don;t have cover merits at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T06:26:06-08:00","id":38701,"title":"","content":"One thing is that the first dot in PT gives you contacts. Which isn't gonna be the case if you wear a different face with those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T07:14:44-08:00","id":38718,"title":"","content":"I would say it could be either, depending on the usage.<br /> <br /> If it's taken as a Demon merit, it applies to a skill-set that was either instilled in you by the God Machine pre-fall, or which you have developed through training with an agency since the fall. The skill set is probably in something related to espionage, demolitions, bureaucracy, or some other Demonesque thing, and the Contact dots represent contacts who are either Demons/Exiles/Stigmatics and KNOW you are a demon, or people you deal with anonymously who won't be put off their game by having a different person show up each week saying &quot;Ecuador sent me, I am the egg man&quot; to identify themselves as a contact.<br /> <br /> If it's taken as a Cover Merit, it applies to a skill-set appropriate to the cover. Maybe you built a patchwork cover out of bits of the lives of a dozen Lawyers. Some sort of bleed through from taking one guys Law Degree and another's junior year at Harvard, and a Third persons Bar Exam. So you pick up little bits and they bleed into the cover and make it better. Mark the bonus Specializations on the Cover, not on your main character sheet. If you take the 4th dot of Profession Training for a Cover, instead of a free skill dot, you get 2 Cover Experience, and if you buy dots in your asset skills you get a Cover Beat instead of a regular beat. If you Burn this cover, or trade it away, or when you aren't using it, your Cover Professional Training bonuses don't apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T07:26:25-08:00","id":38723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38149-is-professional-training-a-demon-merit-or-a-cover-merit?p=38718#post38718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it could be either, depending on the usage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think you could do both?<br /> Say (in your example of a lawyer),<br /> As a demon having cover skills in Stealth, Firearms, Athletics<br /> and as a lawyer cover having skills in Academics, Persuasion and Politics<br /> Then you could get 9 again on oh so many rolls.<br /> (Though mechanically this isn't really that great)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T09:42:44-08:00","id":38766,"title":"","content":"I suppose I would have to house rule that. I mean, you CAN have the same merit as a demon applying to demon things and as a cover applying to cover things, I'm pretty sure that the Demon rules give explicit examples of tracking things like Resources and Contacts separately for Demon and Cover...<br /> <br /> So, I'd make one of two rulings (honestly I'd have to try both out and see which worked better, these are pure theory right now).<br /> 1&gt; If you are in a Cover that has Prof.Train. it overrides your NORMAL (demon)PT while in that Cover. So if you have Demon PT(Spy-Handler) and Cover PT(Longshoreman) then your Longshoreman benefits apply while in cover that cover, and your Demon PT benefits apply while in demon form and/or any OTHER covers that DON'T have a Cover PT.<br /> <br /> 2&gt; Both your DemonPT benefits and current cover's CoverPT benefits apply, <b>but using your DemonPT's benefits causes a compromise roll</b> for acting out of character for your cover. Fillip\u00e9 the Longshoreman's sudden and inexplicable proficiency at filling out and forging CIA mission authorization forms is gonna break cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, probably option 2. Having excessive power at a constant risk to your Cover is sort of a theme for Demon, so I'm gonna go with &quot;Using Non-Cover Profession Training benefits while in Cover causes a Compromise Roll.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}